      "lineNbr": 129,
      "author": {
        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-03-09T01:44:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Including extra triangles is only used in two places\n - the sample slide for convenience (the equivalent middle-out triangles in regular use are drawn with an entirely separate op class)\n - PathInnerTriangulateOp so that it can have breadcrumb triangles written in the stencil buffer\n\nI need to do more digging to see if these triangles are necessary if we write a better triangulator not based on GrTriangulator, or if we can include them some other way\n    \nRegardless, the only real use is PathInnerTriangulateOp and that specifically uses a PathCurveTessellator and not the PathTessellator base class. Wedges aren\u0027t compatible with extra triangles anyways since the extra fan point they include take care of covering the path area. As such, I would rather keep this semi-leaky interaction between PathCurveTessellator and PathInnerTriangulateOp as narrow as possible.",
      "parentUuid": "6f268bbe_c85cd6d0",
      "revId": "d6eefecfaa9834ea3090f3f9f0d577b03b5f4e2b",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
