      "writtenOn": "2022-03-08T18:13:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I had experimented in the omnibus CL with having PathCurveTessellator expose a makeWriter() function that returned its PatchWriter, allowing callers to have control over how the extra triangles were sent to the writer.\n\nI think this is cleaner, since prepareWithTriangles is really only for gpu-v1 and the PathInnerTriangulateOp. Mapping the middle-out triangles manually within a sample seems like a reasonable trade off to me, and allows the curve tessellator\u0027s patch writer definition to be entirely private still.",
